<title>PORTUGAL: Cimpor sale rakes in 120 bln esc.</title>
<headline>Cimpor sale rakes in 120 bln esc.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government earned a total of about 120 billion escudos ($775 million) from the sale of a 45 percent stake in cement group Cimpor-Cimentos de Portugal, a senior government official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The value of the sale was about 120 billion escudos,&quot; Fernando Teixeira Santos, Under-Secretary for Finance, told reporters at a special session at Lisbon bourse to announce details of the sale.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
